            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Among widely sold options, Explore Cuisine's organic black bean and edamame spaghetti lead, at about 25 g and 24 g of protein per 2 oz dry serving respectively, per labels at the time of writing. Kaizen's lupini pasta follows at about 19 to 20 g. Chickpea, lentil and wheat-blend pastas land between 10 and 14 g, compared with about 7 g for regular durum wheat pasta."
