          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is protein pasta good for weight loss?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It can help. Higher protein and fiber make a meal more filling, which may make it easier to eat a sensible portion and stay full longer. Calories per serving are similar to regular pasta, though, so it is not a free pass. Weigh your dry portion, add vegetables and a lean protein, and use it as part of an overall calorie plan rather than a fix on its own."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is Barilla Protein+ gluten-free?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "No. Barilla Protein+ is made with semolina and durum wheat blended with lentil, chickpea and pea flours, so it contains gluten. Barilla's red lentil and chickpea pastas are the brand's gluten-free options. If you need gluten-free, check for a gluten-free claim on the box and read the allergen statement, and see our gluten-free protein powder guide for supplements."
          }
