          </p>

          <p>
            On Amazon, multipacks and Subscribe & Save usually beat single boxes, but watch for listings from third-party sellers charging inflated prices or shipping single boxes as a pack. Our <a href="/amazon-protein-powder/">guide to buying protein on Amazon</a> explains how to spot a dodgy listing; the same checks apply to pasta. Stick with Ships from and sold by Amazon, or the brand's own storefront, and check the per-ounce price before you add to cart.
          </p>
